menu "HomeControl network"

	config HC_WPS_BUTTON_GPIO
		int "GPIO of the WPS button (active low; -1: no button)"
		range -1 48
		default 9 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
		default 0 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
		default -1
		help
			Holding this button for about 3 s starts WPS push-button provisioning. The default is
			the BOOT button of the Espressif devkits (GPIO9 on the ESP32-C6, GPIO0 on the
			ESP32-S3), a strapping pin that is read only after boot. The pin is configured as an
			input with the internal pull-up; pressed means low.

	config HC_WIFI_MAX_TX_POWER
		int "Maximum WiFi transmit power (quarter dBm, 8..84)"
		range 8 84
		default 80
		help
			Passed to esp_wifi_set_max_tx_power() when the station starts: 80 is 20 dBm, the
			driver's maximum; 44 is 11 dBm. A lower value saves supply current during
			transmit bursts: a board on a weak USB supply browns out at full power (the
			development C6 did, doc/hardware.md). Range check and lower values as the chip
			supports them; the driver rounds to the next supported step.

endmenu
